── SYNTAX ERROR ─────────────── E0100_javascript_arrow_function.lt:1:53  [E0100]

Stilt writes a closure as `|x| x * 2`:

  1 │ fn doubled(xs: List<i64>) -> List<i64> { xs.map((x) => x * 2) }
    │                                                     ^^

A closure is its parameters between `|`, then its body: `|x| x * 2`, or `|a, b|
{ … }` for a block.

To fix it, write the closure with `|`:

  1 │ fn doubled(xs: List<i64>) -> List<i64> { xs.map(|x| x * 2) }
    │                                                 ~~~
